\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Training and evaluation loss curves during LoRA fine-tuning for representative models from different architectural families. The decoder-only models LLaMA3-8B and Qwen2.5-7B exhibit rapid and stable convergence, with training and evaluation losses decreasing consistently throughout fine-tuning. In contrast, the encoder--decoder baseline T5-base begins with substantially higher initial loss and converges more slowly. These results indicate that instruction-oriented causal language models adapt efficiently to the proposed urban-science instruction dataset under lightweight LoRA fine-tuning.}}{22}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:training_loss}{{3}{22}{Training and evaluation loss curves during LoRA fine-tuning for representative models from different architectural families. The decoder-only models LLaMA3-8B and Qwen2.5-7B exhibit rapid and stable convergence, with training and evaluation losses decreasing consistently throughout fine-tuning. In contrast, the encoder--decoder baseline T5-base begins with substantially higher initial loss and converges more slowly. These results indicate that instruction-oriented causal language models adapt efficiently to the proposed urban-science instruction dataset under lightweight LoRA fine-tuning}{figure.caption.11}{}}
\newlabel{fig:mc_acc}{{4a}{22}{MC Accuracy}{figure.caption.13}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig:mc_acc}{{a}{22}{MC Accuracy}{figure.caption.13}{}}
\newlabel{fig:sa_bert}{{4b}{22}{SA Paraphrasing}{figure.caption.13}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig:sa_bert}{{b}{22}{SA Paraphrasing}{figure.caption.13}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Comparison of pre- and post-training performance across models. Fine-tuning has heterogeneous effects across architectures. Qwen models maintain near-perfect multiple-choice accuracy, T5-base substantially improves semantic paraphrasing despite failing structured answer selection, and LLaMA3 models achieve notable gains in dataset-specific reasoning accuracy after fine-tuning.}}{22}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:eval_perf_compare}{{4}{22}{Comparison of pre- and post-training performance across models. Fine-tuning has heterogeneous effects across architectures. Qwen models maintain near-perfect multiple-choice accuracy, T5-base substantially improves semantic paraphrasing despite failing structured answer selection, and LLaMA3 models achieve notable gains in dataset-specific reasoning accuracy after fine-tuning}{figure.caption.13}{}}
